          "derivation": "Combine x>=2 with x!=2. The principal root is strictly positive on the resulting domain, so only the numerator zero x=6 solves the equation."
        },
        {
          "label": "f",
          "ordinal": 6,
          "input_latex": "\\frac{6-2x}{9-x}\\sqrt{x-9}=0",
          "domain_latex": "x\\in(9,\\infty)",
